# React components

- **One component function per file.** Never define a second `function` / `const` component in the same file (no local `Rule`, `Kicker`, row, or board helpers next to a page).
- **Pages only compose.** A page file imports sections and returns layout. It does not inline nav, hero, stats, features, boards, CTAs, or footers.
- **Share repeated chrome.** If the design uses the same bar, brand, or footer on multiple screens, put it in `components/` and vary only the slot (`children`). Do not keep a page-named copy (`LandingNav`) of a shared shell.
- **Keep each file small.** One UI concern. If a component grows past ~50 lines of JSX or you need another component to keep it readable, extract a new file.
- **Helpers are not components.** Style factories, constants, and types go in `.ts` files — still one concern per file, never a second component.
- **No inline presentation styles.** Do not use `style={{}}`, Mantine `styles`, or CSS modules for hover or color. Put Tailwind utilities on the element (`className="hover:text-body"`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — chrome copied into a landing-only file
export function LandingNav() { return <Group component="nav">...</Group>; }

// ✅ GOOD — shared shell; page-specific links are children
export function Nav({ children }: { children?: ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <Group component="nav">
      <BrandMark />
      {children}
    </Group>
  );
}
```
